n is proportionally smaller relative to trunk height than in reference-0. In render-0 the crown spread is about 0.35 of the tree height; in reference-0 it is about 0.6. The frond count also looks lower than the 30–60 the inventory estimates. The inventory treats proportions as variation (uncertain).", "The trunk in render-0 is essentially straight. render-1 shows a gentle, single-direction curve in the upper third. render-2 shows only a slight bow. None is wavy, and diameter is near-constant apart from a slight flare at the base.", "The only structures on the trunk are small stub knobs. There are no leaves, branches, epiphytes or other growth on the trunk. The epiphytic ferns in reference-1 and reference-2 are variation, not a target.", "render-3 metadata marks visibility as 'hidden', but the image clearly shows a close-range trunk surface with 4 sparse stubs. I assessed what is drawn. reference-2 is a close-up of the mid/lower trunk, not the ground-level base; the inventory notes that no reference shows the root zone.", "Finish quality is comparable to the spruce anchor's stylised catalogue level. The anchor is used only as a finish floor, not for morphology.", "There is no dead-frond skirt, which is a secondary trait. Frond colour is uniform mid-to-deep green, which falls within the frond-colour-range variation."], "findings": [{"observation": "The crown reads as a palm rosette of arching pinnate fronds in both seeds, with the lowest fronds drooping below the crown base.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Frond length and crown spread relative to trunk height are noticeably smaller than in reference-0, and crown density looks lower. The owner calls frond length a first dial. The inventory treats proportions as uncertain variation, so this is not recorded as a defining mismatch.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond length or leaflet size may still sit toward the low end of the dial range. Also, the trunk is much taller relative to the crown than in reference-0."}, {"observation": "The trunk surface lacks the dense spiral diamond lattice of leaf-base stubs. Only sparse, isolated knobs are drawn.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The inventory says this trait is not yet expressed by the generator. The fn-110 stub organs appear to be placed at low density and small size."}, {"observation": "No fibrous matting appears anywhere on the trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit clusters appear on either seed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The date cluster (fn-111) has not landed, per the owner requirements."}, {"observation": "The trunk is straight or gently leaning, never wavy, and near-constant in diameter in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk. The small stubs are leaf-base organs, not growth.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The P-BASE render is flagged visibility 'hidden' in the metadata, but the image shows the trunk surface at close range. I assessed it on what is drawn.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "There is no dead-frond skirt beneath the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Many pinnate fronds radiate from a single apex. The central ones are upright and the outer ones progressively recurve, giving a rounded shuttlecock outline. The crown is smaller relative to the trunk than in reference-0 and has somewhat fewer fronds; I treat this as proportion variation."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The leaflets are narrow, pointed and spreading, giving a bristly frond margin at catalogue scale. The V-sectioned grouping is only weakly legible, but nothing in the renders contradicts it."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Only sparse, isolated conical knobs sit on a smooth cylinder. There is no tessellating spiral rhomboid lattice of stubs."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The trunk surface is smooth and uniform, with no fibre layer."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "A single unbranched columnar stem of near-constant diameter carries the crown in both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "No fruiting bunches are present. The owner notes that the date cluster (fn-111) has not landed; the trait is still a core mismatch."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system",